@@ -34,6 +34,28 @@ For details of the methods, please refer to the corresponding papers below:
 - [arXiv preprint] Gorgeous: Revisiting the Data Layout for Disk-Resident High-Dimensional Vector Search
 - [NeurIPS'21] SPANN: Highly-efficient billion-scale approximate nearest neighborhood search
 
+### External method adapters
+
+The local `src/BBQ` adapter runs calibrated ADC-BQ (BBQ) with the same dataset
+manifests and emits a compact common result CSV. BBQ remains a separate method
+because its compressed HNSW traversal and final batched FP refinement are not the
+same query path as using ADC-BQ inside DiskANN. See [`src/BBQ/README.md`](src/BBQ/README.md).
+
+### NQ/MSMARCO modern-embedding pilot
+
+`test/run_nq_msmarco_baselines.py` runs the Qwen-1024 NQ and MSMARCO pilot with
+24 build threads and one search thread. It compares a shared FP32-node DiskANN
+graph with PQ64 routing, the same graph with pure 1-bit RaBitQ routing
+(`ex_bits=0`), native PipeANN with 1-bit RaBitQ, and SPANN PQ128 with fixed
+exact FP32 rerank@80. Builds and completed searches are reused on restart.
+
+```bash
+python3 test/run_nq_msmarco_baselines.py --rounds 1
+```
+
+Raw method CSVs, a union table, and the matched Recall@10 0.95/0.99 summary are
+written under `results/nq_msmarco_qwen1024/`.
+
 
